#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d84c2b7-7e87-5003-a0ae-cf907011148a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282093} {:answer/id #uuid "897f2f6b-955d-5a90-b368-aafbe23fc778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282094} {:answer/id #uuid "238b4156-fe38-512b-8174-689e062953d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282095} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1de455-fa3c-55bb-9b6a-8ec1e3f8b163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282096} {:answer/id #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282097} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb73f107-6494-54b1-8438-bfd8864c7ff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb7c4e5a-23fb-5e2d-b89b-6f04ed6e4095" :question/math-academy-id "q-115310" :question/problem "What is the center of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=0$ and $k=-4,$ so the center is located at $(0,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d343ee0c-0bce-549f-a377-d82fee76ecc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282100} {:answer/id #uuid "629b8174-ce7b-5e6f-be8a-18285794a866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d343ee0c-0bce-549f-a377-d82fee76ecc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282100} :answer-field/id #uuid "62b7ea3b-fcb6-5690-8365-0a52be1947eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f5db72a-42be-544f-badf-b1a3297e7c62" :question/math-academy-id "q-278347" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/assets/89914bff0203020e476acedc399cfdcc4a546bac9ee747f01951019e8d85c85d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282104} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbde829e-e840-53ab-8dd2-2f44399375ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282106} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3349205-1811-5815-9329-dbfa5f8bc11b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d364c20-40e0-58aa-a4d5-2b6f9f2f6ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-278401" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{7}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=6$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f8eccc3-9000-5479-b4e9-01c9d24a4c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f8eccc3-9000-5479-b4e9-01c9d24a4c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282109} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1426200-9694-5ad7-bfe1-25419619f01c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78384db2-8f46-5cae-ae65-c8d138abb397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78384db2-8f46-5cae-ae65-c8d138abb397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282111} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da93786-0b28-53b3-bcb9-b8154a490fe2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7a9731a-7828-547b-97be-92ff1076f487" :question/math-academy-id "q-278404" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=-8,$ so the center is located at $(3,-8).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=8$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=8,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6b6a114-fcf4-59dc-8717-07a8f96bfbec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 1)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 3)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086570} {:answer/id #uuid "e09415b9-b0b6-5162-91db-605f6f448c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(8) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(2) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086571} {:answer/id #uuid "2088c170-af4d-5902-9e39-24d71284d87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086572} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd41287-65a2-5acf-8910-60f0222f18de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 3)^{2})/(2) + ((y - 1)^{2})/(8) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086573} {:answer/id #uuid "786d85f2-ff1e-56c8-92ff-879e5ac52192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786d85f2-ff1e-56c8-92ff-879e5ac52192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086574} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa33e9aa-8875-5c99-9a88-261fa19140ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "573849bd-9036-5460-9507-bc3e024db188" :question/math-academy-id "q-7627" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/assets/2ab9745cb9d157e566c101a6ca79514017903fa57eaf8725c846afd272c74f93.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
